{"uid":"e4e6bd03346b1c43","name":"test_spec_and_cli_docs_describe_the_indexed_bounded_tail_read","fullName":"tests.test_hub_real_render_cap_whole_call#test_spec_and_cli_docs_describe_the_indexed_bounded_tail_read","historyId":"26897a77cc5a352e0d50ba1be58b953c","time":{"start":1791867077973,"stop":1791867077976,"duration":3},"description":"Task cure-01-04-2 (D.1; DoD 4, cure-01-04 retry): SPEC.md §11.4 and\n    docs/cli.md must describe the log tail `rendered_log_lines` actually\n    serves -- the `render_index.bounded_tail` read first, a `/logs?tail=1`\n    probe only for the `live` flag, and a bounded `/logs?tail=<bound>`\n    fallback -- but the fallback's own growing-bound re-ask loop has no\n    byte cap and, on a cold or unusable-index run, CAN end up fetching and\n    rendering the entire available transcript for a small POSITIVE `tail`\n    too, not only for `tail=0`. The docs must no longer pin the false\n    'never fetches the whole backlog' claim the review found falsified by\n    the real cold-tail fallback (see\n    `test_a_cold_positive_tail_fallback_can_render_the_entire_backlog_exactly`\n    below); they must instead distinguish the bounded indexed read (cost\n    proportional to `tail`) from the uncapped cold/unusable-index scan\n    (positive-tail fallback may fetch everything), and describe `tail=0`\n    as an explicit whole-transcript request, not the only path that can\n    read the whole thing.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task cure-01-04-2 (D.1; DoD 4, cure-01-04 retry): SPEC.md §11.4 and<br />\ndocs/cli.md must describe the log tail <code>rendered_log_lines</code> actually<br />\nserves -- the <code>render_index.bounded_tail</code> read first, a <code>/logs?tail=1</code><br />\nprobe only for the <code>live</code> flag, and a bounded <code>/logs?tail=&lt;bound&gt;</code><br />\nfallback -- but the fallback's own growing-bound re-ask loop has no<br />\nbyte cap and, on a cold or unusable-index run, CAN end up fetching and<br />\nrendering the entire available transcript for a small POSITIVE <code>tail</code><br />\ntoo, not only for <code>tail=0</code>. The docs must no longer pin the false<br />\n'never fetches the whole backlog' claim the review found falsified by<br />\nthe real cold-tail fallback (see<br />\n<code>test_a_cold_positive_tail_fallback_can_render_the_entire_backlog_exactly</code><br />\nbelow); they must instead distinguish the bounded indexed read (cost<br />\nproportional to <code>tail</code>) from the uncapped cold/unusable-index scan<br />\n(positive-tail fallback may fetch everything), and describe <code>tail=0</code><br />\nas an explicit whole-transcript request, not the only path that can<br />\nread the whole thing.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791866910617,"stop":1791866910618,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791866910618,"stop":1791866910618,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791867077963,"stop":1791867077963,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791867077964,"stop":1791867077966,"duration":2},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791867077966,"stop":